# StreadProV2 — video assets are not committed

`/public/v2/vid/` is in `.gitignore` (23 MB, mostly `15.mp4` at 13.2 MB) —
too large to commit. Everything else under `public/v2/` (images, fonts
reference, the GLB model, the HDR environment, the pre-built JS/CSS
bundle) **is** committed.

After cloning, copy the videos back in manually before `/stread-pro-v2`
will show the gallery's video slides and the `#vid` section correctly:

```
stread-pro-3d-source/public/vid/  →  public/v2/vid/
```

(`stread-pro-3d-source/` itself ships with its own `public/vid/` already —
no rebuild needed for this step, just a copy.)

Without this, the gallery's video thumbnails and the `#vid` scrolling
section will 404 on their `.mp4`/poster `.jpg` sources; every other
section is unaffected.
